{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":494011,"name":"Yudai Ninomiya","username":"Y_David_N","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/y_david_n/{size}/121260_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-17T12:27:18.651Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494011-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494011-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494011-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494011-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAll of my Grok Bots have progressively become unresponsive.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eInitially, only some bots stopped responding. Eventually only one bot remained responsive, but that bot also stopped responding. At this point, none of my existing Grok Bots respond to messages.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eResetting affected bots did not restore them.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis appears to affect multiple independent bots across my Grok Bot fleet rather than one specific bot or conversation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494011-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494011-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen an existing Grok Bot conversation.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSend a simple message to the bot.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe bot does not respond.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRepeat with other existing Grok Bots.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe same behavior occurs across the fleet.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eReset an affected bot and try again.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe bot remains unresponsive.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eObserved progression:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSeveral bots initially became unresponsive.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDreggBot temporarily remained responsive, then also stopped responding.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e“App Development Bot” was the final responsive bot.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eI sent that bot a longer read-only diagnostic instruction.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eImmediately afterward, it also became unresponsive.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eNow no Grok Bot is confirmed responsive.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI cannot confirm whether the longer diagnostic request caused the final failure or merely coincided with an already progressing backend issue.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494011-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494011-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bots should accept messages, create and execute runs, and return responses normally.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eResetting a bot should also restore normal operation if the issue is limited to that bot.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA failure in one bot should not progressively make unrelated bots across the same account/workspace unresponsive.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494011-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494011-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWindows 10/11\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494011-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494011-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWindows 0.55.0\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494011-additional-information-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494011-additional-information-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis appears to be an account/workspace-level or shared Grok Bot execution issue.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eImportant observations:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eMultiple independent bots progressively stopped responding.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eBot reset did not recover affected bots.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe failure eventually affected the last remaining responsive bot.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eNo bot is currently confirmed responsive.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eI have stopped further resets, bot recreation, profile edits, shared-skill changes, and other configuration changes to preserve the current state for investigation.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eI have not directly modified any internal database or backend state.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlease investigate the server-side state for my account/workspace, particularly:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003emessage ingestion / send pipeline\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003erun creation\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003equeue and worker assignment\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eaccount/workspace concurrency limits\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003estuck runs or sessions\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003esession/resource exhaustion\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003erouting\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ebackend locks\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003emodel invocation\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eresponse delivery\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe final responsive bot stopped replying immediately after receiving a longer read-only diagnostic request. I am reporting this as an observation, not claiming it as the root cause.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf possible, please check the final successful and first failed runs server-side and recover any stuck account/workspace runner or session state.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePublic service status showing “Operational” does not match the behavior currently affecting my account.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494011-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494011-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSometimes - I can sometimes use Cursor\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":1,"updated_at":"2026-09-17T12:27:30.431Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":27,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":135.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":172023,"topic_slug":"sev-1-all-grok-bots-unresponsive-after-reset","display_username":"Yudai Ninomiya","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":138424,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/sev-1-all-grok-bots-unresponsive-after-reset/172023/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":494016,"name":"Colin","username":"Colin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/colin/{size}/90452_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-17T12:28:01.197Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003e2 posts were merged into an existing topic: \u003ca href=\"/t/some-of-the-bots-became-unresponsive-failed-to-send-on-my-messages-to-them/171858\"\u003eSome of the bots became unresponsive (failed to send on my messages to them)\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":3,"post_type":3,"posts_count":1,"updated_at":"2026-09-17T12:28:01.197Z","reply_count":0,"reply_